+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Shipped              |
+
+Every tool declares a JSON Schema that is handed verbatim to the providers, and `ToolRegistry` is the one place the engine can hold a model-authored call to it. This spec pins that contract: input is validated against the resolved definition's `inputSchema` inside `ToolRegistry.execute` before the executor runs, a rejected call comes back as a `ToolResponse` the model can read and correct within the tool-round budget rather than as an exception that ends the turn, and neither the rejection nor the log echoes the input the model sent. The full statement of the contract lives here; `src/orchestration/tools/registry.ts` carries a one-line comment pointing at it.
+
+## Rejection before execution
+
+- A call the resolved schema rejects returns a `ToolResponse` whose `result` names the missing required property, and the executor is never invoked ([validated by: rejects a call the schema rejects before the executor runs, naming the missing property](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L24)).
+- Input the schema accepts reaches the executor exactly once and unmodified: no injected default, no coercion, and a property the schema does not list passes through untouched ([validated by: passes a valid call with an unlisted extra property to the executor unmodified, exactly once](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L37)).
+- A wrong-typed value is rejected with a message naming the property path and the expected type, and the message never repeats the offending value back ([validated by: rejects a wrong-typed value naming the path and expected type, without repeating the value](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L55)).
+
+## Schema compilation
+
+- A static tool's schema is compiled once at `register` time, so every later `execute` call is held to the schema as it stood at registration ([validated by: holds a static tool to the schema compiled at register across ten execute calls](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L109)).
+- Registering a tool whose schema cannot compile throws at registration time, where the deployer sees it, naming the tool that carries the broken schema ([validated by: throws at register time for an uncompilable schema, naming the tool](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L73)).
+- A schema produced by a function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` resolves per call, and the call is validated against the schema the source returns for that call, not a stale one ([validated by: validates a function-defined tool against the schema its source returns for that call](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L88)).
+
+## Redaction
+
+- Rejection text and log lines name property paths and the constraints that failed, never property values, so identifying data the model put into a tool call does not enter the log ([validated by: keeps an identifying value out of the rejection text and the log lines](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L128)).
+
+## In the tool loop
+
+- A schema rejection reaches the model as a normal tool result, so `processMessage` resolves rather than throwing, and the provider sees the rejection text on its next round and can retry with corrected input ([validated by: returns a schema rejection to the model as a tool result and lets a corrected retry finish the turn](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L41)).
+- An unknown tool name still throws `Unknown tool: <name>`; validation changes nothing about that failure class, which stays a throw on purpose ([validated by: still throws Unknown tool for an unregistered name](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L122)).
